Why: SpliceAI2 (Illumina, 2026-10) targets quantitative and deep-intronic splice effects, the thesis question; adding it as one more informational predictor lets us compare it with SpliceAI/Pangolin/SPiP on our variants.

To do (option A of walkthrough/20261106_spliceai2_inclusion.md), once you accepted the Hugging Face terms and answered the licence questions in PR-02:
- download only precomputed_scores_v2.0 GRCh38 to /data_lab_PGP/resources/annotation/ (location your OK), check REF alleles against our FASTA on a sample;
- one tabix-indexed file, looked up in VEP_ANNOTATE or a small step;
- columns SpliceAI2_score, SpliceAI2_DS_*/DP_*, SpliceAI2_status (scored / not_covered; not covered is never 0);
- no change to SpliceAI, ACMG or NEW_IMPACT.

Done when: fixture run with the new columns, status counts checked, Module 3 told of the new columns.
